When I first bought this game, I didn't think I would enjoy it as much as I did.
The scenarios and everything else is hand painted, the game is an absolute work of art;
The bosses are gigantic compared to Jora, which makes it feel like a 2D Shadow of the Colossus and shows that you are indeed just a petty mortal trying to impress the gods;
Soundtrack is wonderful and goes very well with the setting of the game;
Combat is very difficult, can be both frustrating or rewarding, that is up to you (git gud).
11/10.   No cons to this game.

This game is no circuitry;
it is electrifyingly fun, gorgeous music, upbeats art, and an overall dark mysterious story.
Play this.

+ great physics engine which allows you to mess around with foes and objects;
+ graphics and music are top notch;
+ an rpg side to it, with upgrades and the ability to learn new skills;
+ story has potential, despite the mostly dull characters;
+ some challenging boss fights;
- short;
- lacks replayability, you can play again with your character maxed out, but feels boring the second time nonetheless;
- some locations are reused (bad move if it's a short game anyways).
TFU has a gimmick, a Jedi game with a fitting physics engine, and exploits it. Good times in spite of its flaws. Recommended.

