Serious Sam 2 isn't a bad game, but it lacks polish and is far from being actually good. In other words, mediocre.
What's wrong with the game? Loads of things.
- bad gunplay : I didn't find shooting toy enemies with toy guns with berely any gore to be fun at all;
- the cartoony artstyle, the childish tone as well as the overused, forced cheap humour made the game less compelling compared to the other Sam games;
- lazily put invisible walls are almost everywhere and are painfully obvious;
- hand-holding;
- cut-down exploration : SS2 tends to feed the player with resources considerably more than the other SS games do, leaving little space for exploration, especially since often areas aren't that big. The secrets are still plenty, though, as well (kinda) creative.
Still, there are definitely some good things that should be mentioned :
- the locales are varied and some are quite interesting (Kleer Planet looks
);
- the soundtrack is rather pleasing as well;
- good enemy variety;
- the game quite manages to recapture the very essence of Serious Sam - the 'Dancing with the enemies' type of gameplay, where enemy, weapon prioritisation and good movement as well as decision making are vital.
SS2 tries to have variety by bringing some new interesting gameplay mechanics, such as vehicles/turrets or some gimmicky levels, but unfortunately most of these are executed poorly and alongside the general problems of the game overshadow the good stuff.
All in all, it's a very imaginitive and creative title - it's obvious that the people who worked on it poured their hearths into it - but it simply falls short as far as design and polish go.

Factorio is an overwhelming game, in the sense that it'll give enough gameplay for a lifetime while still being in early access. If that scares you, don't let it; it continues growing with each passing day, with the devs working on putting out updates on it almost weekly. And you can bet each update adds something new to the game; the newest update that I have had the pleasure to play around with is the nuclear update; it adds a new, fun way to power your factory. As you may have guessed, it's power plants that are powered by uranium. But it doesn't end there; this isn't that type of game. No, you'll find you need to mine uranium, refine it, get two types of uranium, one of which is extremely rare. You can turn the common ones into that rare one, and.... well, it goes on and on. Before you might think this will turn you off, let me assure you. It won't.
The true beauty of factorio can't be experienced in one, singular way. You will feel a multitude of motives, but the point, in this game, is clear; expand. Make your factory bigger, widen it as far as you can. The complexity of this not only adds to the gameplay, it adds to the achievement you will get when you finally launch that rocket into space. But it won't end there. You'll make another factory. And another. This game will pull you in, and it doesn't let go. So there's only one real suggestion I can make before you buy this game;
Have some spare time.

Let's see, what needs to be said about Factorio... well, it's $20, and almost certainly won't be going on sale cheaper than that (see the
). So buy it now. Yes, right now. It's
fantastic.

This is the well-known BBF sequel which made many players reconsider what game to buy, all thank to Dice. I bought this game for almost 5 euros, when Summer Sale 2013 was going on.
This game totally gave me another view upon FPS games, concerning graphics, physics, environment and so on. What is unique about this game is what DICE has been developing for good years>FROSTBITE. A cool thing that makes a good interrelation between Cause and Effect(s). Look for some gameplays/playthrough on YouTube, you will get it easy.
- great environment feeling;
- teamplay;
- variety of weapons which you can customize afterwards;
- variety of vehicles, choppers, tanks- not talking about their particular model of vehicle, but their usage;
- large maps(it's not a 'cozy's camper paradise'- it just fits to all 4 classes available in the game);
- again great teamplay courtesy of each classe's duty;
- great graphics;
- astonoshing real sound.
- can't find any at the moment;
- just to fill this space, the price should be lowered.
All in all, I would recommend it to my friends, fact that I already did it. It still diserves attention even if its successors have domninated the FPS games market. I would have played more but, I don't have that much time left for videogames because of school.
It's a must-have game! COME ON AND GET IT!

